# API Endpoint Reference Documentation

All endpoints are hosted relative to the main API base path: `/api/v1`

---

## 1. Ingestion Component Endpoints

### A. Ingest Website (`POST /api/v1/ingestion/website`)

* **Purpose:**
  Performs real-time BeautifulSoup text scraping of the target URL, executes Gemini-driven automatic document categorization (case study, report, blog, etc.) and industry classification, constructs an energetic active summary, splits text recursively into chunks, generates vector embeddings, inserts them into the `documents` table, and logs the source inside the `knowledge_manifest` table.

* **Request Body Schema (`WebsiteIngestionRequest`):**
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://www.vaco.com/resources/case-studies/outbound-call-center",
    "category": "case-study", // Optional. If omitted, categorized automatically by Gemini.
    "industry": "technology"  // Optional. If omitted, classified automatically by Gemini.
  }
  ```

* **Response Body Schema (`IngestionResponse`):**
  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "Website ingested successfully",
    "chunk_count": 4,
    "logs": [
      "Starting website ingestion...",
      "Scraped 15200 characters.",
      "Successfully inserted 4 rows.",
      "Saved manifest entry."
    ]
  }
  ```

* **Sample cURL Command:**
  ```bash
  curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/ingestion/website" \
       -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
       -d '{"url": "https://www.vaco.com/blog/tips-to-prepare-for-and-manage-technology-disruptions"}'
  ```

---

### B. Discover Sub-routes (`POST /api/v1/ingestion/website/sub-routes`)

* **Purpose:**
  Initiates dynamic sitemap crawler and page analysis (scanning `robots.txt`, sitemap XML indexes, or falling back to raw page anchor tags parsing) to auto-discover and list all crawlable sub-routes starting with the target website root.

* **Request Body Schema (`WebsiteSubroutesRequest`):**
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://www.vaco.com"
  }
  ```

* **Response Body Schema (`WebsiteSubroutesResponse`):**
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://www.vaco.com",
    "sub_routes": [
      "https://www.vaco.com/about",
      "https://www.vaco.com/blog",
      "https://www.vaco.com/services"
    ]
  }
  ```

* **Sample cURL Command:**
  ```bash
  curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/ingestion/website/sub-routes" \
       -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
       -d '{"url": "https://www.vaco.com"}'
  ```

